area()\n1501 | \n1502 |         Area plots are stacked by default. To produce an unstacked plot,\n1503 |         pass ``stacked=False``:\n1504 | \n1505 |         .. plot::\n1506 |             :context: close-figs\n1507 | \n1508 |             >>> ax = df.plot.area(stacked=False)\n1509 | \n1510 |         Draw an area plot for a single column:\n1511 | \n1512 |         .. plot::\n1513 |             :context: close-figs\n1514 | \n1515 |             >>> ax = df.plot.area(y='sales')\n1516 | \n1517 |         Draw with a different `x`:\n1518 | \n1519 |         .. plot::\n1520 |             :context: close-figs\n1521 | \n1522 |             >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\n1523 |             ...     'sales': [3, 2, 3],\n1524 |             ...     'visits': [20, 42, 28],\n1525 |             ...     'day': [1, 2, 3],\n1526 |             ... })\n1527 |             >>> ax = df.plot.area(x='day')\n1528 |         \"\"\"\n1529 |         return self(kind=\"area\", x=x, y=y, **kwargs)\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/plotting/__init__.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/plotting/__init__.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"DataFrame.plot\", \"DataFrame.plot subplots create subplot\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/__init__.py:plot`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `plot`.\n```\n58 | def plot(data, kind, **kwargs):\n59 |     # Importing pyplot at the top of the file (before the converters are\n60 |     # registered) causes problems in matplotlib 2 (converters seem to not\n61 |     # work)\n62 |     import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n63 | \n64 |     if kwargs.pop(\"reuse_plot\", False):\n65 |         ax = kwargs.get(\"ax\")\n66 |         if ax is None and len(plt.get_fignums()) > 0:\n67 |             with plt.rc_context():\n68 |                 ax = plt.gca()\n69 |             kwargs[\"ax\"] = getattr(ax, \"left_ax\", ax)\n70 |     plot_obj = PLOT_CLASSES[kind](data, **kwargs)\n71 |     p