     ValueError\n228 |         If the shapes are not compatible and cannot be broadcast according\n229 |         to NumPy's broadcasting rules.\n230 | \n231 |     See Also\n232 |     --------\n233 |     broadcast\n234 |     broadcast_arrays\n235 |     broadcast_to\n236 | \n237 |     Examples\n238 |     --------\n239 |     >>> np.broadcast_shapes((1, 2), (3, 1), (3, 2))\n240 |     (3, 2)\n241 | \n242 |     >>> np.broadcast_shapes((6, 7), (5, 6, 1), (7,), (5, 1, 7))\n243 |     (5, 6, 7)\n244 |     \"\"\"\n245 |     arrays = [np.empty(x, dtype=[]) for x in args]\n246 |     return _broadcast_shape(*arrays)\n```\n\nFound function `numpy/lib/stride_tricks.py:_broadcast_arrays_dispatcher`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n249 | def _broadcast_arrays_dispatcher(*args, subok=None):\n250 |     return args\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"np.lib.stride_tricks\", \"np.lib.stride_tricks sliding window vectorized applications array manipulation\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound file `numpy/lib/stride_tricks.py`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `stride_tricks`.\nJust show the structure of this file due to response length limitations:\n```\n\n__all__ = ['broadcast_to', 'broadcast_arrays', 'broadcast_shapes']\n\n\nclass DummyArray:\n\n    def __init__(self, interface, base=None):\n...\n\ndef _maybe_view_as_subclass(original_array, new_array):\n...\n\ndef as_strided(x, shape=None, strides=None, subok=False, writeable=True):\n...\n\ndef _broadcast_to(array, shape, subok, readonly):\n...\n\ndef _broadcast_to_dispatcher(array, shape, subok=None):\n...\n\n@array_function_dispatch(_broadcast_to_dispatcher, module='numpy')\ndef broadcast_to(array, shape, subok=False):\n...\n\ndef _broadcast_shape(*args):\n...\n\n@set_module('numpy')\ndef broadcast_shapes(*args):\n...\n\ndef _broadcast_arrays_dispatcher(*args, subok=None):\n...\n\n@array_function_dispatch(_broadcast_arrays_dispatcher, module='numpy')\ndef broadcast_arrays(*args, subok=False):\n...\n\n`