eries/examples/mplot3d/polys3d.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 1 | \"\"\"\n 2 | ====================\n 3 | Generate 3D polygons\n 4 | ====================\n 5 | \n 6 | Demonstrate how to create polygons in 3D. Here we stack 3 hexagons.\n 7 | \"\"\"\n 8 | \n 9 | import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n10 | import numpy as np\n11 | \n12 | from mpl_toolkits.mplot3d.art3d import Poly3DCollection\n13 | \n14 | # Coordinates of a hexagon\n15 | angles = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, 6, endpoint=False)\n16 | x = np.cos(angles)\n17 | y = np.sin(angles)\n18 | zs = [-3, -2, -1]\n19 | \n20 | # Close the hexagon by repeating the first vertex\n21 | x = np.append(x, x[0])\n22 | y = np.append(y, y[0])\n23 | \n24 | verts = []\n25 | for z in zs:\n26 |     verts.append(list(zip(x*z, y*z, np.full_like(x, z))))\n27 | verts = np.array(verts)\n28 | \n29 | ax = plt.figure().add_subplot(projection='3d')\n30 | \n31 | poly = Poly3DCollection(verts, alpha=.7)\n32 | ax.add_collection3d(poly)\n33 | ax.set_aspect('equalxy')\n34 | \n35 | plt.show()\n36 | \n37 | # %%\n38 | # .. tags::\n39 | #    plot-type: 3D,\n40 | #    styling: colormap,\n41 | #    level: intermediate\n42 | \n```\n\nFound `lib/matplotlib/_tight_bbox.py:adjust_bbox`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 1 | \"\"\"\n 2 | Helper module for the *bbox_inches* parameter in `.Figure.savefig`.\n 3 | \"\"\"\n 4 | \n 5 | from matplotlib.transforms import Bbox, TransformedBbox, Affine2D\n 6 | \n 7 | \n 8 | def adjust_bbox(fig, bbox_inches, fixed_dpi=None):\n 9 |     \"\"\"\n10 |     Temporarily adjust the figure so that only the specified area\n11 |     (bbox_inches) is saved.\n12 | \n13 |     It modifies fig.bbox, fig.bbox_inches,\n14 |     fig.transFigure._boxout, and fig.patch.  While the figure size\n15 |     changes, the scale of the original figure is conserved.  A\n16 |     function which restores the original values are returned.\n17 |     \"\"\"\n18 |     origBbox = fig.bb